// The Regency's own structures: the tech 1 core every side fields (factories, mass, power,
// storage, point defence, anti-air, radar, walls), built as Regency machines: dark armour
// plates lapped over bronze machinery that works. They are not ARC's buildings in black:
// each one bends the shared job toward how the Regency fight.
//
// - Excavator: cuts the ore with an excavation beam and needs no power, but costs more
//   mass up front.
// - Power Generator: gravity squeezes plasma to a star's pressure until it fuses; it never
//   explodes, so generators can be packed tight where ARC reactors cannot.
// - Reliquary: one building holds mass and energy both, in three tiers.
// - Picket: a short-ranged brawler, more damage than a Sentinel inside its reach.
// - Canopy: a repeater of bursting bolts that hurts a whole flight, not one plane.
// - Orrery: a shorter radar that sees far more; its floating rings add a tier each.
// - Palisade: slow to build, very hard to cut; sections join into one wall as ARC's do.
// - Ward: a tighter shield than the Aegis, but denser; a prism veil.
//
// Their factories turn out the Regency's own Artificer (its tech 2 and 3 from the factories of
// that tier) and, until the Regency has fighting units
// of their own, the stand-in roster's (ARC) units of their tier, poured by nanite streams
// from fabricator heads whose mounts are in `mc_sim::print_heads`. The land and air
// factories upgrade in place to tech 3, like ARC's. Models: `models::regency::*`,
// authored at the sizes here, so every muzzle and pivot below is the model's own number.
[
    // ---- Factories ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    (
        key: "regency_t1_land_factory",
        name: "Anvil",
        role: "Land Factory",
        tech: 1,
        categories: ["Land", "Factory"],
        health: 4600,
        cost: (mass: 250, energy: 2000, time: 320),
        radius: 46, height: 22, footprint: (8, 8),
        vision: 200,
